# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Caldova Waypoint deployment helper configuration.
#
# The ONLY thing a human provides is the Azure OIDC bootstrap (the AZURE_* identity),
# written once by `make oidc` (scripts/oidc.sh). EVERYTHING else — resource names, API keys,
# the Postgres password, the MSAL app registration, cross-stage endpoints, and the
# change-detection state — is discovered / derived / provisioned / generated by the deploy
# itself. There is no "fill these in" matrix.
#
# This .env only feeds the BEST-EFFORT local `make deploy-all` path. The canonical deploy is
# the GitHub Actions workflow (.github/workflows/deploy.yml), which reads the AZURE_* identity
# from repository VARIABLES+SECRETS (set by `make oidc`) and computes the rest at runtime.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- The one irreducible bootstrap: Azure OIDC identity (set once by make oidc) ----
# In GitHub Actions these live as repository VARIABLES and SECRETS. The OIDC bootstrap
# creates or updates the deploy app/SP and grants the roles needed to provision the
# reference environment. Re-bootstrap idempotently in a fresh tenant with: make oidc
AZURE_TENANT_ID=
AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=
AZURE_CLIENT_ID=
AZURE_LOCATION=swedencentral

# ---- Passthrough label + live-discovery hint (NOT a name anchor) ----
# Existing agent/app resource names may be tool-generated and are discovered at runtime. Deploy-owned
# names may preserve compatibility anchors until the cloud path has been proven end-to-end.
AZD_ENV_NAME=waypoint

# ---- Local-only: sibling checkouts for `make deploy-all` (CI uses reusable workflows) ----
LEDGERFIELD_DIR=../ledgerfield
FORGE_DIR=../forge
WAYPOINT_DIR=../waypoint

# ---- Pinned source refs (what to deploy / change-detect) ----
LEDGERFIELD_REF=main
FORGE_REF=main
WAYPOINT_REF=main

# ---- workflow_dispatch overrides (mirror the GH Actions inputs) ----
# FORCE_ALL=false        # run every stage regardless of change/existence detection
# FORCE_FABRIC=false     # force the Fabric OneLake (re)provision even when unchanged
# ONLY=                  # run ONLY this stage: ledgerfield forge waypoint onelake_upload seed wire
# SKIP=                  # comma-separated stages to force-skip, e.g. forge,wire

# ===========================================================================
# Everything below is COMPUTED by the deploy — do NOT set it. Listed for reference only.
# ===========================================================================
# Provisioned / generated (Azure Key Vault, name kv-keystone-<hash> in the dedicated rg-keystone):
#   waypoint-writer-key / waypoint-reader-key / waypoint-admin-key   (x-api-keys, generate-once)
#   postgres-app-password                                            (generate-once)
# Discovered from live Azure (scripts/discover.sh):
#   forge RG (rg-forge), waypoint RG (waypoint-rg, where waypoint deploys its own app),
#   Foundry endpoint + project url, App Insights resource id, Postgres server name,
#   Log Analytics workspace/RG, MSAL client id, deploy-SP object id.
#   (deploy-owned resource groups host Key Vault + state tags — created idempotently.)
# Fabric/OneLake NAME constants keystone passes (waypoint OWNS the actual provisioning):
#   capacity=waypointcorpus workspace=waypoint-corpus lakehouse=corpus prefix=Files/corpus
#   account_url=https://onelake.dfs.fabric.microsoft.com
# Ensured (scripts/msal.sh): the "waypoint" Entra app reg + Waypoint.Read/Write/Admin app roles
#   (ADDITIVE; existing oauth2 scopes + SPA redirect left intact) + identifier uri; the deployed
#   web FQDN is unioned into the SPA redirect URIs in the wire job (pass 2).
# Computed at runtime: WAYPOINT_FABRIC_ADMIN_MEMBERS_JSON from the deploy SP object id
#   so the deploy identity can assign the workspace to capacity.
# Recorded as Azure RESOURCE GROUP TAGS by record-state (read by the next run's preflight):
#   deployed corpus/agent/app SHAs, seed SHA, OneLake workspace, API/web FQDNs,
#   MSAL client id, and Key Vault name.
# All of the above flow to waypoint's reusable workflow as INPUTS/secrets — keystone sets
# no hard-coded WAYPOINT_*/WAYPOINT_FABRIC_* repo variables of its own.
